{
  "root_cause": "The modal's focus trap always returns focus to the modal element when focus leaves, preventing Shift+Tab from wrapping from the first focusable element (close button) to the last focusable element (delete button).",
  "repair_strategy": "Track the direction of the Tab keypress (Shift+Tab vs Tab) via a _focusDirection flag. In the focus trap, when focus leaves the modal, return focus to the first focusable element for forward Tab or the last focusable element for Shift+Tab, enabling proper circular navigation.",
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Shift+Tab from the first control in the delete confirmation modal will wrap to the last control, allowing reverse keyboard navigation cycles as expected.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "Incorrect direction tracking could misplace focus.",
    "If no focusable elements are found, focus may be lost.",
    "Additional keydown listener may interfere with other scripts listening for Tab on the modal."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "Tab moves focus through close button → input field → cancel button → delete button in order.",
    "Shift+Tab moves focus in reverse order: delete → cancel → input → close button, then wraps from close button to delete.",
    "Modal still returns focus appropriately when focus leaves via mouse click or Escape key.",
    "Escape key continues to close the modal.",
    "Modal initialization and disposal remain functional."
  ],
  "edits": [
